Doenet-Sync-Version: 0.7.28
Doenet-Sync-NumVariants: 1
Doenet-Sync-Hash: d991e20a6bb5bcca
-->
<problem>

<setup>
<selectFromSequence name="b" numToSelect="2" withReplacement="true" from="-10" to="10" exclude="0" />
<selectFromSequence name="a" numToSelect="2" withReplacement="false" from="-10" to="10" exclude="0" />

<select name="x">p q r s u v w x y z P Q R S U V W X Y Z</select>
<math name="lhs" simplify="full">$a[1]*$x+$b[1]</math>
<math name="rhs" simplify="full">$a[2]*$x+$b[2]</math>
<math name="x_involved" simplify="full">$a[1]-$a[2]</math>

<math name="solution" simplify="full">($b[2]-$b[1])/($a[1]-$a[2])</math>
<math name="minus_cx" simplify="full">-$a[2]*$x</math>
<math name="minus_b" simplify="full">-$b[1]</math>
<math name="a_minus_c" simplify="full">$a[1]-$a[2]</math>
<math name="d_minus_b" simplify="full">$b[2]-$b[1]</math>
</setup>

<p>Solve for $x.</p>
<me>$lhs = $rhs</me>
<p><m>$x =</m> <mathInput name="input1" /></p>

<answer>
<award symbolicEquality="true" simplifyOnCompare="numbers" referencesAreResponses="$input1"><when>
  $input1 = $solution
</when></award>
</answer>


<solution>
To solve, we move all terms involving <m>$x</m> to one side of the equation and the constant terms to the other.  We add <m>$minus_cx</m> to both sides of the equation then add <m>$minus_b</m> to both sides of the equation, obtaining
<md>
  <mrow>$a_minus_c$x \amp = $d_minus_b</mrow>
</md>
Dividing through by <m>$a_minus_c</m>, we obtain the solution:
<me>$x = $solution.</me>
</solution>

</problem>